From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:04:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 06/74] phy: ingenic: Disable the supply in power_off() only

The PHY's supply is enabled in power_on() and disabled in power_off(),
but exit() disabled it once more, so every power_off() then exit(), as
the DWC2 driver does on removal or when its probe fails, unbalanced the
regulator:

  WARNING: drivers/regulator/core.c:3262 at _regulator_disable+0xa0/0x1ac
  ...
   regulator_disable+0x50/0x8c
   ingenic_usb_phy_exit+0x30/0x48
   phy_exit+0x54/0xa4
   dwc2_lowlevel_hw_disable+0xd4/0xdc
   dwc2_driver_probe+0x648/0x678

Leave the supply to power_on() and power_off().
---
 drivers/phy/ingenic/phy-ingenic-usb.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/ingenic/phy-ingenic-usb.c b/drivers/phy/ingenic/phy-ingenic-usb.c
index 7e62d4685..d8e5ef302 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/ingenic/phy-ingenic-usb.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/ingenic/phy-ingenic-usb.c
@@ -124,7 +124,6 @@ static int ingenic_usb_phy_exit(struct phy *phy)
 	struct ingenic_usb_phy *priv = phy_get_drvdata(phy);
 
 	clk_disable_unprepare(priv->clk);
-	regulator_disable(priv->vcc_supply);
 
 	return 0;
 }
